caveat**: `mysql_query` returned `Access denied for user 'root'@'localhost'` on every attempt (including `SELECT 1`), so live-data verification was impossible. The SQL follows the exact join paths and filters documented in the semantic network and validated by precedent metrics dw_1692/dw_4527/dw_1212/dw_1758, all of which run against the same tables and join keys.\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a. Tables/columns**: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (`SUBJECT_TITLE`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS`, `OFFER_DEPT_CODE`) joined to SIS_DEPARTMENT (`DEPARTMENT_NAME`, `SCHOOL_NAME`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING`, `DEPARTMENT_CODE`) on `OFFER_DEPT_CODE = DEPARTMENT_CODE`.\n\n**6b. SQL approach**: a `dept_avg` CTE computing `AVG(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS)` over all Mathematics (Course 18) subject rows in SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY (no positivity filter on the average population, per \"all subjects\"); main query filters `DEPARTMENT_NAME='Mathematics' AND DEPARTMENT_CODE='18'`, `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > 0`, `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y'`, and `NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS > avg`; window column `DENSE_RANK() OVER (PARTITION BY d.DEPARTMENT_CODE ORDER BY d.DEPARTMENT_CODE)`. SELECT list exactly: department name, subject title, enrolled count, school name, dense rank. No rounding applied.\n\n**6c. Reasons**:\n- *Data*: SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY is one row per subject per term — no fan-out; NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS exists at subject grain; SIS_DEPARTMENT is one row per department — 1:1 join on department code.\n- *Semantic-network*: column_concept_enrollment_measures decision guide routes \"number of enrolled students per subject offering\" to SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS; concept_department_dimension routes degree-granting/school filters to SIS_DEPARTMENT; concept_subject_offering_facts confirms SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY carries offering department/school.\n- *Business*: dw_1692 (Mathematics, degree-granting, enrolled > dept average on SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY) and dw_4527 (above-average enrollment filter) are direct